  "issue": {
    "id": "I_kwDOBiM5Uc79BmI6",
    "databaseId": 4245054010,
    "number": 3211,
    "title": "reference interfaces recursively prepended with controller name after reconfiguration",
    "url": "https://github.com/ros-controls/ros2_control/issues/3211",
    "body": "**Describe the bug**\nCleaning up and reconfiguring a chainable controller multiple times (`Cleanup` -> `Configure`) prepends the controller name recursively to the reference interface name.\n\nE.g. when the exported reference interface names are \"a\" and \"b\", after the first `Cleanup` -> `Configure` cycle, they will be `my_controller/a`, and after the next cycle `my_controller/my_controller/a`, and so on.\n\n**To Reproduce**\nSteps to reproduce the behavior:\n\n1. Implement the `ChainableControllerInterface`:\n    ```C++\n    class MyController : public controller_interface::ChainableControllerInterface\n    {\n    public:\n      controller_interface::CallbackReturn on_init() override\n      {\n        exported_reference_interface_names_ = {\n          \"a\",\n          \"b\",\n        };\n        reference_interfaces_.resize(exported_reference_interface_names_.size(), 0.0);\n    \n        // [...]\n    \n        return controller_interface::CallbackReturn::SUCCESS;\n      }\n    \n      CallbackReturn on_configure(const rclcpp_lifecycle::State & /*previous_state*/) override\n      {\n        RCLCPP_INFO_STREAM(get_node()->get_logger(), \"Exported reference interfaces:\");\n        for (const std::string & name : exported_reference_interface_names_)\n        {\n          RCLCPP_INFO_STREAM(get_node()->get_logger(), \"  \" << name);\n        }\n        \n        // [...]\n        \n        return controller_interface::CallbackReturn::SUCCESS;\n      }\n    }\n    ```\n    Notice that `exported_reference_interface_names_` is a member of `ControllerInterfaceBase` and not the implementation `MyController`.\n\n2. Repeatedly, do `Cleanup` -> `Configure` via rqt_controller_manager.\n\n3. Notice the output:\n    ```\n    [my_controller]: Exported reference interfaces:\n    [my_controller]:   a\n    [my_controller]:   b\n    [...]\n    [my_controller]: Exported reference interfaces:\n    [my_controller]:   my_controller/a\n    [my_controller]:   my_controller/b\n    [...]\n    [my_controller]: Exported reference interfaces:\n    [my_controller]:   my_controller/my_controller/a\n    [my_controller]:   my_controller/my_controller/b\n    ```\n\n**Expected behavior**\nThe exported reference interface should not change their name after the controller was initialised.\n\n**Screenshots**\nIf applicable, add screenshots to help explain your problem.\n\n**Environment (please complete the following information):**\n - OS: Ubuntu\n - Version Jazzy\n\n**Additional context**\nAdd any other context about the problem here, especially include any modifications to ros2_control that relate to this issue.\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Describe the bug</strong><br>\nCleaning up and reconfiguring a chainable controller multiple times (<code class=\"notranslate\">Cleanup</code> -&gt; <code class=\"notranslate\">Configure</code>) prepends the controller name recursively to the reference interface name.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">E.g. when the exported reference interface names are \"a\" and \"b\", after the first <code class=\"notranslate\">Cleanup</code> -&gt; <code class=\"notranslate\">Configure</code> cycle, they will be <code class=\"notranslate\">my_controller/a</code>, and after the next cycle <code class=\"notranslate\">my_controller/my_controller/a</code>, and so on.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>To Reproduce</strong><br>\nSteps to reproduce the behavior:</p>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Implement the <code class=\"notranslate\">ChainableControllerInterface</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-c++ notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"class MyController : public controller_interface::ChainableControllerInterface\n{\npublic:\n  controller_interface::CallbackReturn on_init() override\n  {\n    exported_reference_interface_names_ = {\n      &quot;a&quot;,\n      &quot;b&quot;,\n    };\n    reference_interfaces_.resize(exported_reference_interface_names_.size(), 0.0);\n\n    // [...]\n\n    return controller_interface::CallbackReturn::SUCCESS;\n  }\n\n  CallbackReturn on_configure(const rclcpp_lifecycle::State &amp; /*previous_state*/) override\n  {\n    RCLCPP_INFO_STREAM(get_node()-&gt;get_logger(), &quot;Exported reference interfaces:&quot;);\n    for (const std::string &amp; name : exported_reference_interface_names_)\n    {\n      RCLCPP_INFO_STREAM(get_node()-&gt;get_logger(), &quot;  &quot; &lt;&lt; name);\n    }\n    \n    // [...]\n    \n    return controller_interface::CallbackReturn::SUCCESS;\n  }\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">class</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">MyController</span> : <span class=\"pl-k\">public</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">controller_interface</span>::ChainableControllerInterface\n{\n<span class=\"pl-k\">public:</span>\n  controller_interface::CallbackReturn <span class=\"pl-en\">on_init</span>() <span class=\"pl-k\">override</span>\n  {\n    exported_reference_interface_names_ = {\n      <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>a<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,\n      <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>b<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,\n    };\n    reference_interfaces_.<span class=\"pl-c1\">resize</span>(exported_reference_interface_names_.<span class=\"pl-c1\">size</span>(), <span class=\"pl-c1\">0.0</span>);\n\n    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">//</span> [...]</span>\n\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> controller_interface::CallbackReturn::<span class=\"pl-c1\">SUCCESS</span>;\n  }\n\n  CallbackReturn <span class=\"pl-en\">on_configure</span>(<span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> rclcpp_lifecycle::State &amp; <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">/*</span>previous_state<span class=\"pl-c\">*/</span></span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">override</span>\n  {\n    <span class=\"pl-c1\">RCLCPP_INFO_STREAM</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">get_node</span>()-&gt;<span class=\"pl-c1\">get_logger</span>(), <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>Exported reference interfaces:<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>);\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">for</span> (<span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> std::string &amp; name : exported_reference_interface_names_)\n    {\n      <span class=\"pl-c1\">RCLCPP_INFO_STREAM</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">get_node</span>()-&gt;<span class=\"pl-c1\">get_logger</span>(), <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>  <span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span> &lt;&lt; name);\n    }\n    \n    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">//</span> [...]</span>\n    \n    <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> controller_interface::CallbackReturn::<span class=\"pl-c1\">SUCCESS</span>;\n  }\n}<span class=\"pl-ii\"></span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Notice that <code class=\"notranslate\">exported_reference_interface_names_</code> is a member of <code class=\"notranslate\">ControllerInterfaceBase</code> and not the implementation <code class=\"notranslate\">MyController</code>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Repeatedly, do <code class=\"notranslate\">Cleanup</code> -&gt; <code class=\"notranslate\">Configure</code> via rqt_controller_manager.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Notice the output:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"[my_controller]: Exported reference interfaces:\n[my_controller]:   a\n[my_controller]:   b\n[...]\n[my_controller]: Exported reference interfaces:\n[my_controller]:   my_controller/a\n[my_controller]:   my_controller/b\n[...]\n[my_controller]: Exported reference interfaces:\n[my_controller]:   my_controller/my_controller/a\n[my_controller]:   my_controller/my_controller/b\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">[my_controller]: Exported reference interfaces:\n[my_controller]:   a\n[my_controller]:   b\n[...]\n[my_controller]: Exported reference interfaces:\n[my_controller]:   my_controller/a\n[my_controller]:   my_controller/b\n[...]\n[my_controller]: Exported reference interfaces:\n[my_controller]:   my_controller/my_controller/a\n[my_controller]:   my_controller/my_controller/b\n</code></pre></div>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Expected behavior</strong><br>\nThe exported reference interface should not change their name after the controller was initialised.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Screenshots</strong><br>\nIf applicable, add screenshots to help explain your problem.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Environment (please complete the following information):</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>OS: Ubuntu</li>\n<li>Version Jazzy</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Additional context</strong><br>\nAdd any other context about the problem here, especially include any modifications to ros2_control that relate to this issue.</p>",
